# ── Environment Variables ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# POLICY: all configuration and secrets live in env files. Env files are NEVER committed —
# only the `.example` templates are. Every rule is written with an explicit `**/` so a new
# project added under apps/ cannot slip past a root-only rule.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.env.local
**/.env.*.local
**/.env.sentry-build-plugin
# Templates ARE committed. Negations must come last, and a negation cannot re-include a file
# whose parent directory is excluded — no project directory is excluded here, so these work.
!**/.env.example
!**/.env.example.*
!**/*.env.example
!env.example

# ── Local databases & data dumps ────────────────────────────────────────
# A local MongoDB data directory was tracked in this repo once: .tmp-mongo/, 367 files and
# 47 MB of WiredTiger data that can contain real documents. Never commit a database directory
# or a dump — they are data, not source.
.tmp-mongo/
**/.tmp-mongo/
mongodb-data/
**/mongodb-data/
dump/
**/dump/
*.bson
*.wt

